  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district; all funds governmental (School Nutrition and Activities are nonmajor governmental funds), so business_type is null. Receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (trimmed p4-5); beginning/ending cash are the total fund balances (p6; all cash). Balance sheet from the cash-basis Statement of Net Position (p3); no liabilities printed. General Fund budget schedule (p8-10) differs from the statement because the statement consolidates the Depreciation Fund into General: GF schedule beginning balance 8,348,432 + Depreciation 256,025 = statement 8,604,457; and the 250,000 General-to-Depreciation transfer is hidden in schedule line 2700 Student transportation (355,267 vs 105,267 on statement) and eliminated. Other differences: statement Regular instruction 3,439,758 = 3,118,127 + 3500 categorical 165,899 + 6000 federal 155,732; Other support services 75,971 = 21,220 + Depreciation disbursements 54,751. Detail records the General Fund schedule as printed with the 2700 line split (spending 105,267, transfer -250,000) and the transfer 850,000 as other financing; the printed total 9,018,544 includes transfers. Budget-only lines with no actual (3500 budget lines 3535, 4518, purchased services/general supplies/equipment in Nutrition) are omitted. Single 'Debt service' line not split into principal and interest. Read pages 1-10 and 11-14 of 14 (Read pages 1-14 of 14)."
